  "question": {
    "text": "For the first order reaction given below select the set having correct statements<br />\r<br />\r<math><mn>2</mn><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>5</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">4N</mi><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>+</mo><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">g</mi></mrow></mfenced></math><br />\r<br />\r(1) the concentration of the reactant decreases exponentially with time<br />\r<br />\r(2) the reaction proceeds to 99.6 % completion in eight half life duration<br />\r<br />\r(3) the half life of the reaction depends on the initial concentration of the reactant<br />\r<br />\r(4) the half life of the reaction decreases with increasing temperature"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "1,2",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1,2,3",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "1,2,4",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "1,2,3,4",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Here for this reaction statements 1,2 and 4 are correct as follows<br/><br/>For first order reaction <br/><br/> <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></mrow></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn></mrow></msub><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo><mtext>kt</mtext></mrow></msup></math> <br/><br/>Hence concentration of  <math><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\" separators=\"|\"><mrow><mtext>N</mtext><msub><mrow><mtext>O</mtext></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>  decreases exponentially (First  statement is correct).<br/><br/>Also,  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.693</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></mfrac></math> . Which is independent of concentration and  <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msub></math>  decreases with the increase of temperature.<br/><br/> <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>99.6</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.303</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">loglog</mi></mrow><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>0.4</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mfenced></mrow></mrow></math> <br/><br/> <math><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>99.6</mn></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2.303</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mfenced separators=\"|\"><mrow><mn>2.4</mn></mrow></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mo>×</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.693</mn></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn><mi mathvariant=\"normal\"> </mi><msub><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">t</mi></mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msub></math> <br/><br/>So statements 2 and 4 are also correct."
  }
